{"id":"G1377","lemma":"διώκω","transliteration":"diōkō","sayIt":"diōkō","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to pursue","meaning":"διώκω\n[in LXX chiefly for רָדַף ;]\n1. to put to flight, drive away: Mat.23:34.\n2. to pursue;\n(a) of persons; with accusative, without hostility, to follow after: Luk.17:23; with hostile purpose: Act.26:11, Rev.12:13. Hence, to persecute: Mat.5:10-12, 44 10:23, Luk.11:49 21:12, Jhn.5:16 15:20, Act.7:52 9:4-5 22:4, 7-8 26:14-15 Rom.12:14, 1Co.4:12 15:9, 2Co.4:9, Gal.1:13, 23 4:29 5:11 6:12, Php.3:6, 2Ti.3:12;\n(b) metaphorically, with accusative of thing(s), of seeking eagerly after: Rom.9:30, 1Ti.6:11, 2Ti.2:22; νόμον δικαιοσύνης, Rom.9:31; τ. φιλοξενίαν, Rom.12:13; εἰρήνην, Heb.12:14, 1Pe.3:11; τὰ τῆς εἰ., Rom.14:19; τ. ἀγάπην, 1Co.14:1; τὸ ἀγαθόν, 1Th.5:15; absol., to follow on, drive, or speed on (Æsch.), Php.3:12, 14.†\n(AS)","glosses":["persecuted","persecute","pursue","persecuting","do you persecute","persecute you"],"count":44,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":10,"renderings":{"bsb":"are persecuted","kjv":"are they which are persecuted"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":11,"renderings":{"bsb":"persecute you","kjv":"persecute"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"they persecuted","kjv":"persecuted they"}},{"chapterId":"mat-5","v":44,"renderings":{"bsb":"persecute","kjv":"persecute"}},{"chapterId":"mat-10","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"they persecute","kjv":"they persecute"}},{"chapterId":"mat-23","v":34,"renderings":{"bsb":"persecute","kjv":"persecute"}},{"chapterId":"luk-11","v":49,"renderings":{"bsb":"they will persecute"}},{"chapterId":"luk-17","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"chase after them"}},{"chapterId":"luk-21","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"persecute you","kjv":"persecute"}},{"chapterId":"jhn-5","v":16,"renderings":{"bsb":"began to persecute","kjv":"did"}},{"chapterId":"jhn-15","v":20,"renderings":{"bsb":"they persecuted","kjv":"they have persecuted"}},{"chapterId":"act-7","v":52,"renderings":{"bsb":"t